    "Recommended logging schema keeps logs in durable, queryable storage such as a data warehouse or Langsmith.",
    "The core record should have one row per turn or event.",
    "conversation_id is a unique id for the whole conversation.",
    "session_id is a session-level id if multiple conversations per session are possible.",
    "user_id should be an anonymized user identifier, not raw PII.",
    "turn_id is an incremental id within a conversation, or can be a timestamp plus sequence.",
    "timestamp stores the event timestamp in ISO format.",
    "role can be user, assistant, system, or tool.",
    "content_masked stores text after PII masking.",
    "raw_metadata stores other non-PII metadata such as model name, prompt id, latency, channel, and client app.",
    "model_output stores the assistant’s response, masked if needed.",
    "event_type can be message, escalation, email, rating, system_event, or similar.",
    "status can be completed, in-progress, or escalated.",
    "storage_location is a pointer or URL to a full conversation blob if stored separately.",
    "pii_masked_fields is a list of fields or types masked in the record, such as phone, card, address, Aadhaar, or DOB.",
    "retention_policy is a label for how long the record should be kept.",
    "Late-signal or attachment records should be stored as separate rows that reference a core conversation.",
    "event_id is a unique id for a late signal.",
    "conversation_id links the late signal back to the original conversation.",
    "original_turn_id optionally identifies which turn the signal is associated with.",
    "signal_type can be escalation, support_email, refund_request, followup_survey, or similar.",
    "signal_timestamp records when the late signal actually occurred or was observed.",
    "signal_payload_masked stores masked text or metadata for the signal.",
    "link_metadata describes how the signal was linked, such as email, manual match, or automated heuristic.",
    "Logging should be asynchronous so conversation flow is not delayed.",
    "The log record should be produced locally and enqueued or sent to the logging service in the background while the response is delivered to the user.",
    "The logging path should not add request-path latency.",
    "Logging should be treated as parallel asynchronous I/O to Langsmith or the warehouse.",
    "The logging side should use durable delivery with retries and acknowledgement so async logging is not lossy.",
    "Final logs should be stored in a durable backend such as a data warehouse or observability tool like Langsmith.",
